If the characteristic and the consistency test are primitive recursive, then the code-level gated step is primitive recursive.

The outer first unpairing, the inner first unpairing, and the second unpairing of the outer first unpairing are primitive recursive by the left and right projections. Their pairing is primitive recursive. Composition with the characteristic and the consistency test, then with the one-test and multiplication, gives the condition. The presentation's intersection of those two components is primitive recursive by composition with the primitive-recursive intersection, after identifying the paired arguments by unpacking. Primitive-recursive selection of the condition, the intersection, and the accumulator, identified by reflexivity, is the code-level step.
